    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Pairs of (Julian date, equivalent ISO/Gregorian date) used to verify that {@link JulianChronology#date(java.time.temporal.TemporalAccessor)} converts an ISO {@link LocalDate} back to the correct {@link JulianDate}. The Julian calendar differs from the Gregorian calendar by 2 days in year 1 and gradually shifts to 13 days by the 20th century, because the Julian calendar adds a leap day every 4 years without exception while the Gregorian calendar skips century years that are not divisible by 400."
